course: dictionary
lesson: 6885
title: Overseas and other countries
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Overseas» means in or to another country, especially one across the sea. In «my cousin lives overseas», the word tells you where your cousin lives: in a country on the other side of the sea.
explain: The word can also describe things. In «overseas students», it is an adjective: it tells you the students come from another country. Look at the word after it to find its job: a person, a place or a thing.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in «abroad» or «in another country». «We are going overseas» and «We are going abroad» both make sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: Overseas means in or to another country, especially one across the sea.
fact: As an adverb it tells you where something is: «my cousin lives overseas».
fact: As an adjective it describes something: «overseas students» are students from another country.
fact: «France uses 12 time zones, more than any other country, if its overseas territories are counted.»
fact: Gibraltar, one of the British Overseas Territories, has been British since 1704 and guards the entrance to the Mediterranean.
exercise: «My cousin lives overseas.» What does overseas mean here? | Under the water | Next door to her house | In a tall building | *In another country, across the sea
exercise: «She welcomed the overseas visitors to the school.» What does overseas describe? | Visitors who came by car | Visitors who are very old | *Visitors from another country | Visitors who are very tall
exercise: Find and copy the word that means in or to another country: «France uses 12 time zones, more than any other country, if its overseas territories are counted.» | france | *overseas | time | counted
test: Mum says, «We are going overseas this summer.» What does overseas mean? | Round the garden | Under the bed | *In another country, across the sea | In the car park
test: Gibraltar is one of the British Overseas Territories. What does overseas tell you about these territories? | *They are outside the UK, in other parts of the world | They are under the sea | They are very old castles | They are inside the UK
exam: Priya says overseas means only the sea. What is the correct meaning? | A very small island | Only the sea and the fish in it | *In or to another country, especially one across the sea | A ship that sails at night
